      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "```js\nconst TUNING={\ncar:{\nmaxSpeed:62,     // m/s top speed without boost\naccel:18,        // m/s² at full throttle\nbrake:34,        // m/s² braking deceleration\ndrag:0.0037,     // per m: dv -= drag*v*v each second\nrolling:0.06,    // per s: dv -= rolling*v each second\nsteerRate:2.2,   // rad/s yaw rate at low speed\nsteerAtSpeed:0.42,// share of steerRate left at maxSpeed (linear between)\ngrip:8.5,        // per s: decay rate of sideways velocity\ndriftGrip:2.2,   // per s: sideways decay while drifting\ndriftSteer:1.4,  // steerRate multiplier while drifting\nboostFill:0.34,  // meter 0..1 filled per s of valid drift\nboostSpeed:74,   // m/s top speed during boost\nboostSeconds:1.8,// s of boost from a full meter\nwallSlow:0.62,   // speed multiplier on wall contact\nbump:5.5         // m/s impulse split between cars on contact\n},\nai:[\n{name:\"VOLT\",color:\"#ff2bd6\",skill:1.03,aggression:0.75},\n{name:\"NOVA\",color:\"#00f0ff\",skill:1.015,aggression:0.55},\n{name:\"RAZOR\",color:\"#ffe600\",skill:1.0,aggression:0.9},\n{name:\"HALO\",color:\"#7cff4f\",skill:0.985,aggression:0.35},\n{name:\"EMBER\",color:\"#ff7a1a\",skill:0.97,aggression:0.6}\n],\nrace:{laps:3,countdown:3,rubberBand:{range:80,behind:0.08,ahead:0.04}},\ncamera:{\ndistance:7.5,    // m behind car\nheight:2.6,      // m above car\nlag:0.12,        // s smoothing time constant\nfovBoost:12      // degrees added to FOV at full boost\n}\n};\n```\n\n1. Flow: Title (Enter/tap START) → countdown 3-2-1-GO (1 s per step, inputs locked, throttle revs only) → race for `laps` laps → results podium when the player crosses the line on the final lap (unfinished rivals ranked by progress) → \"Race again\" resets the grid and timers.\n2. Physics: every frame `v += (accel*throttle - drag*v*v - rolling*v)*dt`, which levels off near 62 m/s. Boost raises the cap to `boostSpeed` and multiplies accel by 1.5. Shift spends the meter (it needs at least 0.25), and a full meter lasts `boostSeconds`.\n3. Drift start: hold Space while steering above 18 m/s. Grip changes to `driftGrip` and steering is multiplied by `driftSteer`. The meter fills at `boostFill` per second only while speed is above 25 m/s and the slip angle is above 0.15 rad.\n4. Drift end: releasing Space, falling below 12 m/s, or hitting a wall ends the drift. A wall hit also cuts speed by `wallSlow` and gives no meter.\n5. Checkpoints: N gates sit about 60 m apart in track order, and only the car's next gate index counts. Passing gate 0 after gate N-1 adds a lap. Progress = `lap*N + gate + fraction to the next gate`, and positions are sorted by progress every frame.\n6. Wrong way: if the dot product of heading and track tangent is below -0.3 for 1.5 s at more than 5 m/s, show WRONG WAY. The warning clears once the dot product is above 0.3. Gates passed backwards never count.\n7. Rubber band: a rival more than `range` metres of progress behind the player gains up to 8% top speed, and one more than `range` ahead loses up to 4%. Both scale linearly from 0 at `range` to the full value at 2×`range`. Rival top speed = `skill × maxSpeed`, and each rival brakes to its own corner speed.\n8. Unverified: the pacing targets (about 52–56 s per clean lap on 1.8 km, VOLT 2–6 s behind a good drifting player, a non-drifting player beaten by VOLT and NOVA) come from arithmetic estimates only. Nothing was run or playtested, so retune `skill`, `boostFill` and `steerAtSpeed` against the built track."
