      "output": "**Status: not actually run.** I read the source only. Nothing was loaded, rendered, played or measured, and no network request was observed.\n\n**Confirmed in source**\n- **Tuning:** the `TUNING` block matches upstream exactly.\n- **Physics:** acceleration uses `accel*th - drag*v|v| - rolling*v`. Boost sets the cap to `boostSpeed`, multiplies accel by ×1.5, needs at least 0.25 meter and drains over `boostSeconds`. The player's cap is 1×`maxSpeed`.\n- **Drift:**\n  - Starts when steer > 0.2 and speed > 18 m/s.\n  - Uses `driftGrip` and `driftSteer`.\n  - The meter fills only above 25 m/s with slip > 0.15 rad.\n  - Ends on Space release, below 12 m/s, or a wall hit. The wall hit applies `wallSlow` on first contact.\n- **AI:**\n  - Rubber band is linear from `range` to 2×`range` (+8% behind, −4% ahead).\n  - Brakes from look-ahead curvature.\n  - Offsets its lane around cars less than 14 m ahead.\n- **Race flow:**\n  - Positions are re-sorted every frame. Results are triggered by the player finishing, with rivals ranked by finish time, then progress.\n  - The 3-2-1-GO countdown locks movement and revs the engine. Race again rebuilds the grid.\n  - Touch buttons for ◀ ▶ GAS BRAKE DRIFT BOOST use pointer capture.\n- **Rendering:** the PMREM environment comes from the sky scene. The chain is RenderPass → UnrealBloomPass(.65, .45, .85) → OutputPass, with ACES tone mapping.\n\n**Defects found**\n1. **External request:** `\"three\":\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.186.1/...\"`. The import map fetches from a public CDN instead of the AwwO-supplied r186 modules. `RoomEnvironment` is imported but never used, which adds an extra fetch.\n2. **Bump impulse cancels out:** `a.vx+=nx*(rel/2)-nx*C.bump/2` and `b.vx-=nx*m` with `m=rel/2+C.bump/2`. Both cars receive −n·bump/2, so there is no separating impulse. B's term should be `+C.bump/2`.\n3. **Wrong-way timer:** `if(c.ww>1)c.wrongWay=true` uses 1 s; the rule says 1.5 s.\n4. **Checkpoints:** `Math.floor(c.s/(L/8))%8` gives 8 gates of about 225 m, not gates about 60 m apart. `TRACK.checkpoints` is never used. Progress is computed as `lap*L+s`, not `lap*N+gate+fraction`.\n5. **Meter fills on the wall:** holding Space against a wall re-arms `c.drift` and fills the meter in `_rDrive` before `_rRoad` cancels it. This breaks the \"wall gives no meter\" rule.\n6. **No real mirroring:** the asphalt (roughness .35) reflects only the sky environment. Nothing mirrors the neon, so the wet-asphalt look is not met.\n\n**Unverified (needs an actual run)**\n- Whether `three@0.186.1` resolves and all seven addon paths load.\n- Whether the shader compiles and the frame rate holds.\n- Bloom and visual appearance.\n- Whether the modules and wiring match the upstream deliverables as pasted.\n- Lap pacing (52–56 s) and AI competitiveness.\n- Collision feel and overtaking.\n- Behaviour on touch devices.\n- Audio.\n- Correct lap counting over three full laps.\n- Race again repeated multiple times."
